00:21:28,871 --> 00:21:29,955
Come on.

244
00:21:33,543 --> 00:21:34,795
- What's going on?
- Nothin'.

245
00:21:34,878 --> 00:21:38,424
The guy's punchin' on the breaks.
Just take care of it. We're fine.

246
00:21:40,468 --> 00:21:42,846
I can't see nothin', man.
Just go and cut 'em off, Angie.

247
00:21:42,888 --> 00:21:45,725
No, no. You can't fight
with no gloves on.

248
00:21:46,559 --> 00:21:48,520
Just get up. Get up.
Try and do it. Come on.

249
00:21:48,562 --> 00:21:51,023
I can't see, man.

250
00:21:51,065 --> 00:21:53,735
- Come on, Cass!
- Dance!

251
00:22:00,410 --> 00:22:02,412
Liston crouching,
hitting to the body.

252
00:22:02,495 --> 00:22:05,457
It's like he's blinking,
like he doesn't see Liston.

253
00:22:05,541 --> 00:22:08,127
Ref, you gotta doy our job.

254
00:22:17,848 --> 00:22:18,891
Hold it.

255
00:22:21,894 --> 00:22:24,272
Stay away from him, Clay.
Stay away from him.

256
00:22:25,065 --> 00:22:27,443
The champion, you can see,
is the aggressor.

257
00:22:33,909 --> 00:22:35,828
- Get him, Cass!
- Come on, Cass!

258
00:22:36,913 --> 00:22:39,416
- Knock him up!
- Clay looks all done.

259
00:22:39,499 --> 00:22:41,502
Hold on to him!

260
00:22:45,715 --> 00:22:48,510
- Stop it. Stop. Break.
- Knock him up.

261
00:22:51,889 --> 00:22:54,309
Get on him.
Get on him, man.

262
00:23:11,497 --> 00:23:14,459
- You can see him now.
- You go get him, man.

263
00:23:25,598 --> 00:23:28,101
Clay lands a left,
but Liston ducked under it...

264
00:23:28,184 --> 00:23:30,437
and took it high
on the forehead.

265
00:23:31,396 --> 00:23:33,607
It's Clay coming on.

266
00:23:38,530 --> 00:23:41,242
And Liston backs away.

267
00:24:26,923 --> 00:24:30,636
And all the predictions
are going down the drain...

268
00:24:30,719 --> 00:24:32,638
as Liston is listless.

269
00:24:35,016 --> 00:24:36,810
And there's the bell.

270
00:24:39,730 --> 00:24:41,649
We're coming up to round seven.

271
00:25:19,988 --> 00:25:22,324
Wait a minute!

272
00:25:22,408 --> 00:25:24,202
Liston's not coming out.

273
00:25:25,203 --> 00:25:28,499
The winner and new heavyweight
champion of the world is Cassius Clay.

274
00:25:28,582 --> 00:25:32,629
Eat your words!
Eat your words!

275
00:25:32,670 --> 00:25:36,467
Les, I'm going up into the ring.
Get back.

276
00:25:37,677 --> 00:25:40,055
I'm the greatest thing
ever happened to boxing.

277
00:25:40,138 --> 00:25:41,974
Cassius. Cassius.

278
00:25:42,015 --> 00:25:44,602
I shook up the world!

279
00:25:44,685 --> 00:25:47,939
It's a scene of
absolute bedlam in the ring!

280
00:25:48,023 --> 00:25:52,278
I am the greatest.
I'm a bad man. I shook up the world!

281
00:25:52,361 --> 00:25:54,072
Did he ever hurt you?

282
00:25:54,155 --> 00:25:57,159
I'm only 22 years old.
I ain't got a mark on my face.

283
00:25:57,201 --> 00:25:59,161
- I must be the greatest.
- And you're pretty.

284
00:25:59,203 --> 00:26:01,164
I must be the greatest.

285
00:26:01,206 --> 00:26:04,501
Wait. Hold on. Hold on one second.
That's Sam Cooke back there.

286
00:26:04,543 --> 00:26:06,504
- Come on, Sam Cooke.
- Let Sam Cooke in here.

287
00:26:06,545 --> 00:26:09,466
The greatest rock-and-roll singer,
and I'm the world's greatest boxer.

288
00:26:09,549 --> 00:26:11,051
Hello, Sam.

289
00:26:19,979 --> 00:26:22,148
That mummy's
gonna get him, baby.

290
00:26:22,982 --> 00:26:25,402
- That mummy ain't gonna get him.
- Yeah, he is.

291
00:26:25,485 --> 00:26:29,741
He ain't scared of that mummy.
That mummy too slow to catch anybody.

292
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:33,328
- What's going on, Sam?
- How you doing, Cassius?

293
00:26:33,412 --> 00:26:37,876
Don't believe that stuff on TV.
Don't listen to him.

294
00:26:37,917 --> 00:26:40,045
- Hey, congratulations, Clay.
- Hey, thank you, Jim.

295
00:26:40,128 --> 00:26:43,132
- Hell of a fight.
- You next, man. You next.

296
00:26:43,215 --> 00:26:46,511
- Go ahead and get some food, brother.
- Cassius Clay versus Jim Brown.

297
00:26:46,595 --> 00:26:48,013
Biggest fight in history.

298
00:26:48,096 --> 00:26:51,225
- The mummy only has one eye.
- One eye and a limp.

299
00:26:51,267 --> 00:26:53,895
That mummy's 643 years old.

300
00:26:53,937 --> 00:26:55,898
He can't catch nobody.
Look at him.

301
00:26:55,939 --> 00:26:59,152
You gotta fall down 'cause that's
the only way the mummy could catch you.

302
00:27:10,666 --> 00:27:12,126
Way to go, champ!

303
00:27:14,796 --> 00:27:18,217
- Yeah, you the greatest.
- Thank you, brother. Thank you.

304
00:27:18,300 --> 00:27:20,261
- I'll see your next fight.
- You'll see the next one?

305
00:27:20,344 --> 00:27:23,181
- Oh, yeah.
- Well, you better get there very early.

306
00:27:23,265 --> 00:27:26,268
You better get there very early
'cause that man's going down.

307
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:31,608
If he talk a little jive,
he's going down in five.

308
00:27:33,527 --> 00:27:36,489
He talk a little more,
I might drop him in four.

309
00:27:37,616 --> 00:27:39,785
If you wanna have more fun,
do it in round one.

310
00:27:39,868 --> 00:27:41,954
Oh, yeah. Hold on.
I'm doing the rhymin'.

311
00:27:55,972 --> 00:27:59,226
The people really look up to you. You
plan on being a champ like Joe Louis?

312
00:27:59,309 --> 00:28:02,271
Well, yeah, I'm gonna be
the people's champ.

313
00:28:02,354 --> 00:28:04,732
Not like Joe Louis.
Well, you know, not exactly.

314
00:28:07,194 --> 00:28:09,321
My name is not Clay.

315
00:28:09,363 --> 00:28:11,950
Clay is the name of the people
that owned my ancestors...

316
00:28:12,033 --> 00:28:15,037
and I no longer wanna be called
by that slave name.

317
00:28:15,120 --> 00:28:17,373
- I am Cassius X.
- Minister Malcolm.

318
00:28:17,456 --> 00:28:19,709
What about the divisions
in the Nation of Islam?

319
00:28:19,793 --> 00:28:23,797
This is the champ's time. I'm here
as a friend to support his victory...

320
00:28:23,881 --> 00:28:26,342
so I have nothing you want.

321
00:28:26,384 --> 00:28:28,386
I'm definitely gonna be
the people's champion...

322
00:28:28,428 --> 00:28:30,889
but I just ain't gonna be the champ
the way you want me to be the champ.

323
00:28:30,973 --> 00:28:33,393
I'm gonna be the champ
the way I wanna be.

324
00:28:44,573 --> 00:28:47,201
For no home is immune
to termites...

325
00:28:47,243 --> 00:28:50,372
no matter how well
it is built or maintained.

326
00:28:50,455 --> 00:28:52,416
- Hey, brother.
- I was leaving.

327
00:28:52,499 --> 00:28:55,753
I saw your light on.
What you doing up at this hour, champ?

328
00:28:55,837 --> 00:28:59,591
Oh, man, I'm watching this program
on termites.

329
00:28:59,675 --> 00:29:03,930
And them little itsy-bitsy things is
eatin' these people's whole house down.

330
00:29:04,014 --> 00:29:06,725
Oh, man, look.

331
00:29:09,854 --> 00:29:14,610
I've been invited to speak
at Ibadan University in Nigeria.

332
00:29:14,652 --> 00:29:17,363
- You wanna go with me?
- Hey, look, man.

333
00:29:17,447 --> 00:29:21,577
You can have six million termites
in your house and don't even know it...

334
00:29:21,619 --> 00:29:24,580
till you going to get something to eat
and you bust through the floor.

335
00:29:26,458 --> 00:29:30,212
- What'd you say? Where?
- Africa. You been?

336
00:29:31,297 --> 00:29:32,215
Africa.

337
00:29:32,298 --> 00:29:34,634
All right, come on.
Let's go.

338
00:29:40,225 --> 00:29:41,810
What is it?

339
00:29:46,316 --> 00:29:48,902
You ever thought you'd lose it?

340
00:29:48,985 --> 00:29:51,739
I mean, really lose it?

341
00:29:55,577 --> 00:29:59,332
When I was little, I tore out
this picture of Emmett Till.

342
00:29:59,415 --> 00:30:01,334
They put the barbed wire
around his neck...

343
00:30:01,417 --> 00:30:05,589
and strapped him
to that 75-pound cotton gin fan.

344
00:30:05,673 --> 00:30:09,511
And they cut out one of his eyes
'cause he looked at some white lady.

345
00:30:11,346 --> 00:30:13,307
Man.

346
00:30:13,349 --> 00:30:16,436
I couldn't take my eyes to it,
couldn't throw it away.

347
00:30:21,025 --> 00:30:23,945
When I heard about those...

348
00:30:24,029 --> 00:30:26,991
four little girls who got bombed
in that Birmingham church...

349
00:30:30,203 --> 00:30:32,914
the prohibitions of the Honorable
Elijah Muhammad prevented me...

350
00:30:32,998 --> 00:30:35,251
from speaking
my thoughts in action.

351
00:30:37,253 --> 00:30:39,464
Because Birmingham was part
of the civil rights struggle.

352
00:30:39,548 --> 00:30:43,761
You know, begging for our place
at the white man's table.

353
00:30:43,845 --> 00:30:46,515
But dead children
are dead children.

354
00:30:46,598 --> 00:30:51,145
So the anger I felt
I had to contain.

355
00:30:53,064 --> 00:30:56,151
I locked it up so tight...

356
00:30:56,235 --> 00:30:58,154
my muscles seized.

357
00:30:59,322 --> 00:31:02,242
I lost control
over the right side of my body.

358
00:31:02,326 --> 00:31:04,745
My leg gave out.

359
00:31:04,829 --> 00:31:07,540
Right arm gave out.
"I'm having a stroke," I thought.

360
00:31:09,126 --> 00:31:12,254
But I had to hold it in
'cause all I wanted...

361
00:31:12,338 --> 00:31:16,802
Brother, all I wanted to do
was find something and break it.

362
00:31:16,885 --> 00:31:20,056
Break a part...
Break any part of this system...

363
00:31:20,139 --> 00:31:24,353
because you are so provoked
in your heart...

364
00:31:24,436 --> 00:31:26,564
and your spirit
as a human being...

365
00:31:28,483 --> 00:31:30,444
at dead children.

366
00:31:32,112 --> 00:31:34,198
And I could do...

367
00:31:36,785 --> 00:31:38,537
nothing.

368
00:31:46,964 --> 00:31:50,718
Everyone knows
I can't do nothing...

369
00:31:50,802 --> 00:31:52,220
anymore.

370
00:31:56,726 --> 00:32:00,272
So Elijah Muhammad has suspended me
as a minister in the Nation of Islam.

371
00:32:08,782 --> 00:32:11,619
Man...

372
00:32:11,661 --> 00:32:13,204
you can fix that.

373
00:32:13,288 --> 00:32:16,166
I don't know.

374
00:32:16,208 --> 00:32:18,503
I'll try when we get back.

375
00:32:26,721 --> 00:32:28,765
You get some rest, champ.

376
00:32:28,849 --> 00:32:30,768
All right, brother.

377
00:33:06,061 --> 00:33:07,021
Sit.

378
00:33:19,411 --> 00:33:24,041
You know, only after
long service and high merit...

379
00:33:24,083 --> 00:33:28,547
in the spiritual and physical rebirth
of Afro-American people...

380
00:33:28,589 --> 00:33:30,841
is one granted an original name.

381
00:33:30,925 --> 00:33:33,678
But you are special.

382
00:33:33,762 --> 00:33:35,222
A world champion.

383
00:33:37,767 --> 00:33:40,395
So there is a gift
I wish to give you.

384
00:33:40,437 --> 00:33:42,439
From this day forward...

385
00:33:42,481 --> 00:33:46,986
you will be known
as Muhammad Ali.

386
00:33:51,158 --> 00:33:53,536
- What?
- That's right.

387
00:33:53,619 --> 00:33:55,539
You what?

388
00:33:58,042 --> 00:34:01,754
Well, what's wrong with our name?
My name?

389
00:34:01,796 --> 00:34:04,132
We... We made you.

390
00:34:04,216 --> 00:34:05,676
Ain't nobody made me.

391
00:34:05,759 --> 00:34:07,887
No bow tie-wearin',
Arab-talkin' nigger gonna change that.

392
00:34:07,970 --> 00:34:09,889
Ain't nobody in that ring but me.
I made me.

393
00:34:09,973 --> 00:34:12,476
You don't know who you are.

394
00:34:12,559 --> 00:34:15,313
I know who I ain't.
I ain't drinkin'.

395
00:34:15,396 --> 00:34:17,691
I ain't going back on my wife
and for sure I ain't prayin'...

396
00:34:17,774 --> 00:34:19,943
to no blond-haired,
blue-eyed Jesus.

397
00:34:19,985 --> 00:34:23,948
Paintin' those blue-eyed, blond-haired
Jesuses is what put food in you.

398
00:34:24,032 --> 00:34:26,702
- Steak and vegetables on the table.
- It's dinner!

399
00:34:32,334 --> 00:34:34,253
Go ahead.

400
00:34:35,379 --> 00:34:36,714
Go ahead.

401
00:34:58,658 --> 00:34:59,909
Hello?

402
00:35:00,827 --> 00:35:03,372
Here you go, Daddy.

403
00:35:03,455 --> 00:35:04,999
Thank you, baby.

404
00:35:05,041 --> 00:35:07,502
- Yeah?
- Brother Malcolm.

405
00:35:07,544 --> 00:35:11,590
The Honorable Elijah Muhammad has given
the Muslim name of Muhammad Ali...

406
00:35:11,674 --> 00:35:14,427
to Cassius X.

407
00:35:14,511 --> 00:35:17,931
Herbert Muhammad has been put
in charge of his training.

408
00:35:18,015 --> 00:35:20,268
He will not be traveling
with you to Africa.

409
00:35:20,351 --> 00:35:22,979
He also asked me
to inform you...

410
00:35:23,063 --> 00:35:26,066
that your suspension
will be extended indefiinitely.

411
00:35:36,705 --> 00:35:39,166
Brother Cassius
won't be coming to Africa.

412
00:35:42,754 --> 00:35:44,714
Not with me.

413
00:35:48,678 --> 00:35:50,805
Don't put it off.

414
00:35:56,062 --> 00:35:57,981
We'll be fine.

415
00:36:03,112 --> 00:36:04,489
I will.

416
00:36:04,572 --> 00:36:07,743
I got a little doll
for Atallah.

417
00:36:07,784 --> 00:36:08,869
Really?

418
00:36:08,952 --> 00:36:10,579
Yeah, it? s beautiful.

419
00:36:10,621 --> 00:36:13,458
I've got so much
to show the girls when I get back.

420
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:15,919
- I'm taking alot of pictures.
- Yeah?

421
00:36:15,961 --> 00:36:18,297
Yeah, I got some good stuff
I want to show you.

422
00:36:18,381 --> 00:36:20,300
Are you eating?

423
00:36:21,301 --> 00:36:23,888
Well, you're not cooking, so...

424
00:36:23,971 --> 00:36:26,599
- What's going on? Anything?
- Nothing.

425
00:36:27,559 --> 00:36:29,686
He's on the phone,
talking to his wife.

426
00:36:29,770 --> 00:36:32,940
She's having a hard time sleeping,
the baby's kicking a lot...

427
00:36:33,024 --> 00:36:35,318
what are they gonna
name the baby.

428
00:36:38,155 --> 00:36:42,202
I just wake up a couple of times
in the night, but it? s okay.

429
00:36:54,800 --> 00:36:57,178
Would you like to take a seat?

430
00:36:57,220 --> 00:36:59,181
Sure, thank you.

431
00:37:02,852 --> 00:37:05,063
What y'all done did
with the real pilot?

432
00:37:05,147 --> 00:37:08,025
I am the pilot.
He's the copilot.

433
00:37:08,067 --> 00:37:10,028
Here. Sit down, Mr. Clay.

434
00:37:10,069 --> 00:37:12,489
Oh, man.

435
00:37:12,531 --> 00:37:16,494
In Louisville, where I growed up,
they barely let black folks drive buses.

436
00:38:56,325 --> 00:38:57,576
Muhammad!

437
00:39:01,039 --> 00:39:04,835
Hey, brother.
What's going on, man?

438
00:39:09,007 --> 00:39:10,968
- What you doing here?
- I was just going to the airport.

439
00:39:11,010 --> 00:39:13,638
We just got here now.
So where you going?

440
00:39:13,680 --> 00:39:14,639
Liberia.

441
00:39:14,681 --> 00:39:18,143
Say hello to Maya Angelou right here
and Ambassador Huang Hua.

442
00:39:18,185 --> 00:39:21,022
And that is Taher Kaid.
He's the ambassador from Algeria.

443
00:39:21,105 --> 00:39:24,276
Oh, man. Where should I go?
I wanna go all over this place.

444
00:39:24,359 --> 00:39:26,487
Go to Algeria.
See Ben Bella.

445
00:39:26,570 --> 00:39:30,867
Then go to see Mecca and Medina.
I just came from there.

446
00:39:30,951 --> 00:39:33,287
Made my seven circuits
around the Kaaba.

447
00:39:33,370 --> 00:39:36,499
I prayed at sunrise. Two million people.
Pilgrims from all over, man.

448
00:39:36,541 --> 00:39:39,712
Dressed the same.
High and low, the same.

449
00:39:39,795 --> 00:39:43,633
Blond-haired, blue-eyed Muslims,
Arabs, Africans, Indonesians.

450
00:39:58,443 --> 00:40:01,363
Seeing brothers just like us,
praying together, it was beautiful.

451
00:40:01,405 --> 00:40:03,449
I drank water
from the well of Zem Zem.

452
00:40:03,532 --> 00:40:08,580
I prayed in the ancient city of Mena.
I prayed on Mount Arafat.

453
00:40:08,664 --> 00:40:11,083
You shouldn't have quarreled
with Elijah Muhammad.

454
00:40:12,418 --> 00:40:14,629
Walking in their footsteps.

455
00:40:14,713 --> 00:40:16,340
All of us together.

456
00:40:16,423 --> 00:40:19,260
You shouldn't have quarreled
with the Honorable Elijah Muhammad.

457
00:40:20,094 --> 00:40:21,721
What?

458
00:40:22,890 --> 00:40:26,310
You shouldn't have quarreled
with Elijah Muhammad.

459
00:40:26,394 --> 00:40:28,897
Hey, Brother Muhammad,
look here.

460
00:40:33,236 --> 00:40:35,155
Brother Muhammad!

461
00:40:57,390 --> 00:40:59,393
Listen, I'm sorry
to keep you waiting.

462
00:41:13,493 --> 00:41:15,120
Into each life...

463
00:41:15,204 --> 00:41:17,248
a little rain must fall.

464
00:41:17,331 --> 00:41:20,210
And, you know,
every day cannot be sunny.

465
00:41:20,293 --> 00:41:22,963
Every smile is not
a smile of happiness.

466
00:41:23,005 --> 00:41:24,507
And every tear that is shed...

467
00:41:24,549 --> 00:41:26,801
Sonji, Sonji, Sonji.

468
00:41:26,843 --> 00:41:30,598
- What you keep saying my name for?
- 'Cause I love it, girl.

469
00:41:30,681 --> 00:41:33,059
- How long you been working with Herbert?
- About a year.

470
00:41:33,143 --> 00:41:36,021
I sell Muhammad Speaks
over the phone.

471
00:41:36,105 --> 00:41:39,901
- What kind of name is that?
- My father named me after Sonja Henie.

472
00:41:41,027 --> 00:41:42,988
What's your father do?

473
00:41:43,030 --> 00:41:47,160
He was shot in a poker game
when I was two, so he don't do nothing.

474
00:41:47,243 --> 00:41:49,663
And my mother died
when I was eleven.

475
00:41:49,705 --> 00:41:52,583
- Who raised you?
- My godparents.

476
00:41:52,667 --> 00:41:56,672
But I been off on my own
for a long time.

477
00:41:57,798 --> 00:41:59,759
What you doing tomorrow?
Go for a ride with me.

478
00:41:59,842 --> 00:42:02,303
- Oh, no, no. I gotta work.
- I'm gonna square it with Herbert.

479
00:42:02,387 --> 00:42:05,265
- Herbert said you met the Beatles.
- Oh, yeah, yeah.

480
00:42:05,349 --> 00:42:08,353
Only one of 'em is smart, though.
The fella with the glasses.

481
00:42:08,394 --> 00:42:10,564
